{
 "_readme": "The character factory (docs/briefs/character-factory.md; tools/blender/factory.py). One base head made from MakeHuman's base mesh (CC0): `base` is what every factory man has (targets that make the small forms readable at ~8 mm squares, and `forms`, shaping done by script on the regions MakeHuman's own targets move). A man is a people.json entry with \"source\": \"factory\": an `archetype` from here, his own `targets` on top, a `hair`, `moustache` and `beard` style from here, `skin`, `brows`, `wear` and an `outfit`. Targets are MakeHuman paths (makehuman/data/targets, no extension) and weights; \"{s}\" stands for both sides (r and l). Styles are made once and fitted to any head by the same script; the head's UV layout is laid out once from the base head, so anything drawn on it works on every man.",
